.TH FS-REPORT 1 "October 2026" "SASD Freeware" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
fs-report \- report directory entry counts and logical file sizes
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B fs-report
.RB [ --top " N" ]
.RB [ --min-size " SIZE" ]
.RB [ --one-file-system ]
.I DIRECTORY
.SH DESCRIPTION
Recursively enumerate a directory tree without changing files or following symbolic links.
Report regular files, directories, symlinks, other entries, total logical bytes,
and the largest files.
Hard-linked pathnames contribute separately to logical byte totals.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --top " N"
Show at most N largest files (0 to 1000, default 10).
.TP
.BI --min-size " SIZE"
Only include files at or above this size in the largest-file list.
SIZE is bytes with optional binary K, M, G, or T suffix.
.TP
.B --one-file-system
Skip entries with a different device ID from the starting directory.
.TP
.B --help
Show usage.
.TP
.B --version
Show version.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 complete; 1 traversal errors and potentially incomplete report;
2 invalid arguments; 3 invalid or inaccessible root.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR largefiles (1),
.BR fs-usage (1),
.BR find (1),
.BR du (1)
